            "key_investigations.3",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "risk_assessment.0"
          ],
          "text": "At assessment, suicidal ideation was active with thoughts of overdose — no formed plan or intent, but escalating — and no psychotic features were identified. Risk to self was assessed as moderate-high; protective factors included her two children (ages 8 and 11), help-seeking behaviour, and future orientation. No immediate safeguarding concerns were raised, though the social context was noted for further exploration. By Day 3 suicidal ideation had become passive, and by Day 5 MDT review mood was improving with only fleeting passive ideation and no intent. Sertraline 50 mg once daily was commenced on Day 3 (20/05). Psychoeducation was provided and a collaborative safety plan was completed with the patient.",
