          ],
          "text": "You came into hospital because you had been feeling very low for 6 weeks. You were also not enjoying things you usually enjoy, waking early, eating less, and finding it hard to concentrate. The team diagnosed a depressive episode."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team spoke with you carefully about how you were feeling. Over the days you were with us, your mood began to lift and things felt a little easier.\n\nWhile you were here, the team:\n\n- Started you on a medicine called sertraline on Day 3 (20/05).\n- Gave you information about depression and how it can affect you.\n- Worked with you to make a safety plan."
        },
